{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>At the morning watch.</b> Rashi explained, and I say: since the night is divided into watches, because of the song of the ministering angels, therefore it is called אשמורה. The meaning: because they wait and watch when to say song — I say that they are called אשמרות in the sense of waiting, as in 'his father kept הדבר' (ואביו שמר את הדבר)." "<b>At the morning watch.</b> Near daytime, at the hour when people watch and await the morning." "<b>In a pillar of fire and cloud.</b> At the hour when the pillar of fire withdraws and the pillar of cloud comes, at that time they mingled together one with the other in front of the camp of Egypt. The Egyptians were not accustomed to see a pillar of fire, only the pillar of cloud and darkness at night, and when they saw this they were thrown into confusion by a great noise, for they were shouting to turn the chariots back. But Israel needed neither the pillar of cloud nor the pillar of fire, and they had no need to veer right or left, for the water was a wall for them on their right and on their left."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:52.405408139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}